Step 1: Calculate the number of magazines in one bookshelf. Bryan has 46 magazines in each bookshelf.
Step 2: Calculate the total number of magazines. Since Bryan has 10 bookshelves, the total number of magazines can be calculated by multiplying the number of magazines in one bookshelf by the total number of bookshelves. total_magazines = 46 * 10 = 460

Answer: \boxed{460}
